# Next.JS Rules

## Architecture & Routing
- Use Next.JS 14 with app router. Don't use deprecated pages router.
- Use middleware for all auth-related and security checks.
- Prefer server-side rendering where possible.
- Don't use file system and fs module. It is unavailable.

## Server Components & Actions
- Use Next.JS 14 Server Actions for data mutations and forms.
- When creating Next.JS server action, make sure "use server" is added in the top of that file.

## Client Components
- Add "use client" to each client-side component. This includes code with interactivity like buttons.
- Use useMemo/useCallback for performance-critical components.
- Use Lucide react for icons (already installed)

## Performance & Optimization
- Use Next.js Image component for optimized image loading.
- Implement loading skeletons in loading.tsx file for all routes when required.

## SEO & Metadata
- Always implement relevant metadata tags in layout.tsx/jsx file.
- Use dynamic metadata generation based on route parameters and data.
- When adding new public page than needs to be indexed, add it to src/app/sitemap.ts/js

## Error Handling
- Implement error handling to log full errors on the server and show user-friendly error messages in the UI.

# TailwindCSS & Shadcn/ui Rules

- All components should be optimized for mobile
- Use shadcnui components when available. They can be installed by running `npx shadcn@latest add button`
- Use `@tailwindcss/typography` module and `prose` class when displaying markdown or want to display vanilla HTML elements like h1 h2 etc.
- All components should fully support dark mode

